.TH LUXAFOR-PANEL 1 "" "luxafor-status" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luxafor-panel \- pick the Luxafor light status, optionally for a while
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luxafor-panel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luxafor-panel
opens a small window showing the current status and the running timer,
with one button per status and a choice of durations.
.PP
Pick a duration first \(em
.B \(if
(no timer, the default), 15 or 30 minutes, 1 or 2 hours, or a custom
number of minutes \(em then click a status: it is applied and the window
closes. With a duration, the light goes back to the default status at the
end (see
.BR luxafor-toggle (1)).
.PP
The window also cancels a running timer, and opens the status
configuration. It closes after an action, with Esc, or with its close
button. Launching it again while it is open brings it to the front.
.PP
It is in the application menu as
.BR "Luxafor Panel" ,
in the tray icon's menu as
.B "Other duration..."
(a middle-click on the icon also opens it), and in the
right-click menu of the
.B Luxafor
launcher.
.PP
It follows the desktop's light or dark style, unless the
.B theme
setting (see
.BR luxafor-toggle (1))
forces
.BR light " or " dark .
.PP
When it opens, it also starts the tray icon
.RB ( luxafor-tray (1))
and the call detection
.RB ( luxafor-callwatch (1))
if they aren't running \(em right after installing the package, for
instance \(em unless their autostart was turned off.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR 1 \(en 9
Pick the first to ninth status.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the window.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR luxafor-toggle (1),
.BR luxafor-tray (1)
